@startsalt
' Screen: Rubric List
' User Stories:
'   - As a test engineer, I can browse all rubrics to find one for my evaluation run
'   - As a test engineer, I can create a new rubric to define scoring criteria
'   - As a test engineer, I can see the published version and judge model at a glance
'   - As an admin, I can see rubric status (draft vs published) without opening each one

{
  {
    <b>codefre.sh</b> | Scripts | Prompts | Rubrics | Personas | Runs | Settings
  }
  ==
  {
    <b>Rubrics</b>
    ..
    Evaluation rubrics define scoring criteria and scale types applied by judge models during test runs.
  }
  ==
  {
    [+ New Rubric] | " Search rubrics...          " | ^All Domains^  | ^Any Status^
  }
  --
  {#
    <b>Name</b>              | <b>Slug</b>                  | <b>Scale Type</b> | <b>Published Ver</b> | <b>Judge Model</b>        | <b>Created</b>    | <b>Actions</b>
    RAG Faithfulness       | rag-faithfulness           | Ladder (5pt)  | v3               | gpt-4o-mini            | 2026-04-01  | [View] [Edit] [...]
    Code Quality           | code-quality               | Continuous    | v1               | claude-3-5-sonnet      | 2026-04-12  | [View] [Edit] [...]
    Safety Screening       | safety-screening           | Ladder (3pt)  | —                | gpt-4o                 | 2026-05-08  | [View] [Edit] [...]
  }
  --
  {
    " " | <i>Showing 3 of 3 rubrics</i> | " " | [< Prev] | Page 1 of 1 | [Next >]
  }
  --
  {
    <b>Scale Types:</b> <i>Ladder</i> = discrete ordered labels (e.g. Excellent / Good / Fair / Poor / Fail).  <i>Continuous</i> = numeric range (e.g. 0.0–1.0).
  }
}

@endsalt
